  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 9245df71d6 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures, scratchpad stale1025b/repro_<ID>/). CURRENT, wider than filed. Edge.meta['receiver'] now takes 11 values (adds 'self' ruby ~567 via WI-misir, 'declared_type' cpp ~2056 via WI-lamij; UsageContext receiver metadata in js_ts/py/go excluded) with 2 readers (linkers/method_call_recovery.py:362 '== field_chain'; receiver_blind_magnets.py:177 'in _RECEIVER_MARKERS'), not 1. The registry prose 'complete current producer vocabulary (no consumer branches on it yet)' (axis_meta_keys.py:498-515) is stale and omits qualified/self/declared_type. LIVE CONSEQUENCE of the unguarded vocabulary, filed as WI-sibup (P2): _RECEIVER_MARKERS lacks declared_type, so C++ `Logger lg; lg.Close();` is demoted by finalize to cpp:external:Close:unresolved (0.4) while lg.Flush() survives (reproduced). resolution_quality now takes 8 values (adds accessor_name, py _orm_resolution_quality since 2026-09-10) with 3 readers (receiver_blind_magnets.py:174, verify_claims.py:4520, :4674); 'ambiguous' carries at least three meanings (2026-10-21 audit F2) plus WI-sibup's wrongful demotion -- not covered by WI-sakum (confidence re-derivation). The resolution_quality half overlaps WI-botam facet B (vocabulary normalisation): coordinate or fold. Related: WI-kosup (no-reader sweep). P3 kept."  # 1c85
