  message: "WI-kosup sweep decision (2026-10-28; /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/kosup_reader_census_10282026/B_meta.md §3b). meta['receiver']: OK -- 11 values, both readers' value sets match the producers', and an existing partition test guards it (the keep-with-trigger on it fired and was acted on). meta['resolution_quality']: WIRE -- 7 values and every reader value is written, but the value set is declared nowhere, so the magnet detector's != 'ambiguous' treats any new value as 'receiver identified', and typed / typed_receiver / type_inferred look like synonyms no production reader tells apart. Action: declare the value set (a bounded-enum with its values) with a partition test, as receiver has, and fold or distinguish the three typed spellings. This item now carries that action."  # e4a3
